          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            When we define
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+categories"} internal categories
            of some category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+spans"} category of spans
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Span
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Span}(\mathcal{C})
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+functors"} internal functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colax+morphism"} colax
            monad morphisms) give us
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+functors"} internal functors
            directly: we need to ask that the 1-cell of the morphism is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Span
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Span}(\mathcal{C})
            (which corresponds to asking that the left leg of the span be the identity, or an isomorphism). (This is related to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor#Properties"} behaviour of profunctors
            in that they correspond to functors (via the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints"} left adjoints
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Span
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span(\mathcal{C})
            we
            %em don’t
            require this left-adjoint condition then we end up constructing
            %strong Mealy morphisms
            between internal categories.
          %p
            ‘Mealy morphisms’ are named after
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mealy+machines"} Mealy machines
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+H.+Mealy"} George H. Mealy
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{A}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}
            be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{V}, I, \otimes)
          %p
            A
            %em Mealy morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
