              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Pare12"} Paré 2012
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion of Mealy morphism between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
            was introduced in the paper:
          %ul
            %li#Pare12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Par%C3%A9"}> Robert Paré
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Mealy Morphisms of Enriched Categories
              %strong 20
              (2012) pp 251–273, doi:
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-010-9238-8"}> 10.1007/s10485-010-9238-8
              \.
          %p Mealy morphisms are mentioned in Example 16.8 and Example 16.27 in the paper:
          %ul
            %li#GarnerShulman16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"}> Richard Garner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"} Michael Shulman
              = succeed "," do
                %em Enriched categories as a free cocompletion
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.3191"} arXiv:1301.3191
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2015.11.012"} doi:10.1016/j.aim.2015.11.012
          %p
            Mealy morphisms are also considered under the name “two-dimensional partial map” (a notion attributed to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere"} Lawvere
          %ul
            %li#LackStreet02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Lack"}> Stephen Lack
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
              = succeed "," do
                %em The formal theory of monads II
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-4049%2802%2900137-8"} doi:10.1016/S0022-4049(02)00137-8
          %p Some talk slides which mention Mealy morphisms:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Par%C3%A9"}> Robert Paré
              ,
              %a{:href => "https://www.mscs.dal.ca/~pare/June2010.pdf"} Mealy Morphisms for Tensor Categories
